nor-roll student, but dropped out of school at the age of 17 and began working for a small-time crack cocaine dealer in Virginia. As a teen he would freestyle rap on the streets of Brooklyn. After making a demo tape with neighborhood friends and connections, this demo was eventually received DJ Mister Cee (from Big Daddy Kane). From there he got notice in Hip-Hop magazine, The Source, in the Unsigned Hype section. Sean \"Puffy\" Combs got a hold of the demo tape and after meeting signed Biggie to Uptown Records. Puffy eventually started his own music label, Bad Boy Records, bringing Biggie with him. Soon after Bad Boy's premiere he released the album, Ready To Die, eventually selling over 4 million copies. To this day B.I.G. is regarded as one of the best lyricist ever in Hip-Hop along with his one time friend and eventual adversary, Tupac Shakur.\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:65049","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":261878,"name":"Biggie Smalls"},{"id":643218,"name":"Christopher Wallace"},{"id":6998784,"name":"Frank White (33)"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["(Notorious) BIG","B I G","B.I G","B.I.G","B.I.G.","B.I.G. Notorious","B.i.g","BIG","BIGGIE","Big","Big Intro","Big Papa","Big Pappa","Big Popa","Big Poppa","Biggie","Biggie (The Notorious)","Biggie Smalls","Biggie Smallz","Bigie","B•I•G","G. Big","Motorious B.I.G","Mr. B.I.G.","Natorius B.I.G.","Natorius BIG","Nortrious B.I.G","Not. B.I.G.","Notorios B.I.G.","Notorious","Notorious B 1 G","Notorious B.","Notorious B. I. G.","Notorious B.I.G","Notorious B.IG","Notorious B1G","Notorious BIG","Notorious BIG.","Notorious Big","Notorious Big Poppa","Notorious Big, The","Notorious, BIG","Notorious, Big","Notoriout B.I.G.","Notoriuos B.I.G.","Notorius","Notorius B.I.G","Notorius B.I.G.","Notorius BIG","Notorius Big","Notrious B.I.G.","Notrious BIG","Popa","The NOTORIOUS B.I.G","The Nororious B.I.G.","The Notoriou B.I.G","The Notorious","The Notorious (BK'z Finest)","The Notorious B I G","The Notorious B.I.B.","The Notorious B.I.G","The Notorious B.I.G.","The Notorious B.IG.","The Notorious BIG","The Notorious Big","The Notorious Biggie Smallz","The Notorius B.I.G.","The Notorous B.I.G.","The Notourius B.I.G.","The Notrious B.I.G.","The Notrious BIG","the notorious B.I.G.","the notorious BIG","聲名狼籍先生"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/65049-Notorious-BIG","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.facebook.com/NotoriousBIG","http://www.notoriousonline.org/","http://www.myspace.com/notoriousbig","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Notorious_B.I.G.","https://youtube.com/@notoriousbig?si=1g-z0Xz6jvPCDp70","https://www.instagram.com/thenotoriousbig/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/663496/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"663496","image":"https://i.discogs.com/rTWOpNrXnrF9Jd8JPRoFvrv6CKZkTCauR3tz32vmNLs/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:333/w:373/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTY2MzQ5/Ni0xMjIzNzYwOTU4/LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/caYVBscewnld2b5J0AKIIHD4OrlEeQwSgQTI1nLfugc/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTY2MzQ5/Ni0xMjIzNzYwOTU4/LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Violeta Parra (born October 14, 1917 in San Carlos de Itihue, Chile) was a notable Chilean folklorist and visual artist. She set the basis for [i]Nueva Canción Chilena[/i], a renewal and a reinvention of Chilean folk music. Parra revived the [i]Peña[/i], (now known as [i]La Peña de Los Parra[/i]), a community center for the arts and for political activism. Her most renowned song, [i]Gracias a la Vida[/i], was popularized throughout Latin America by [a=Mercedes Sosa] and later in the US by [a=Joan Baez]. It remains one of the most covered Latin American songs.\r\n\r\nFrom 1949 to 1952 she formed a duo with her sister, [a=Hilda Parra]: \"Las Hermanas Parra\". She also had other brothers dedicated to music, as [a=Roberto Parra], [a=Lautaro Parra], [a6638886] and [a=Lalo Parra], or poets, as [a=Nicanor Parra]. She was also mother of [a=Isabel Parra], [a=Angel Parra] and [a4371254], and grandmother of [a=Tita Parra], [a=Angel Parra (2)] and [a=Javiera Parra].\r\n\r\nVioleta Parra committed suicide with a gunshot on February, 5, 1967, in Santiago, because of her depression over the breakup of her relationship with [a=Gilbert Favre].\r\n\r\nAlong with [a=Gabriela Pizarro] and [a=Margot Loyola] she´s considered one of the most important, central, essential and former members of the chilean folklore history and the duty of collecting, testify (recording) and investigate the origins, develop and richness of the native rural music of her country. \r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:663496","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":[{"active":true,"id":3845891,"name":"Las Hermanas Parra"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["Para","Parra","Parra Sandoval Violeta","V. Larra","V. Para","V. Parra","V. Parra Sandoval","V. Parra-Sandoval","V.Parra","Victoria Parra Sandoval","Violeta","Violeta Pakka","Violeta Para","Violeta Para Sandoval","Violeta Parr","Violeta Parra Sandoval","Violeta Parra Sandval","Violeta Parrová","Violeta Perra Sandoval","Violeta Sandoval Parra","Violeta y Grupo Acompañante","Violetta Para","Violetta Parra","Violetta Parra Sandoval","Violette Parra","Violeyta Parra","В. Пара","Виолета Пара","ビオレータ・パラ","ヴィオレータ・パラ"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/663496-Violeta-Parra","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.violetaparra.cl/","http://www.nuevacancion.net/violeta/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Violeta_Parra","http://www.memoriachilena.cl/602/w3-article-7683.html","http://www.musicapopular.cl/3.0/index2.php?op=Artista&id=24"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/76894/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"76894","image":"https://i.discogs.com/bZV6gYp4KD6p64m-NgFlVEranOuKK-bAXULrvEg5tzA/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:381/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTc2ODk0/LTE2OTY5NTUyOTkt/MTYxNi5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/Io8tq7Hhx2T0cD81wGg57YxlQ8